    "Float expression orders against the reference's: enumerate the spellings of a function's float expressions.\n"
    "\n"
    "Usage:\n"
    "  float_order.exe <unit> <Name> [--target T] [--address 0x..] [--minutes 5] [--workers N] [--line N]\n"
    "                  [--max-site 400] [--quiet] [--full-unit] [--tree-only] [--normal-priority]\n"
    "  float_order.exe --batch [--select REGEX] [--units a,b] [--wall body] [--minutes 3] [--jobs N]\n"
    "                  [--workers 3] [--limit N]\n"
    "  float_order.exe --selftest\n"
    "(every form also takes --root DIR and --config FILE: the project adapter, config/ctools.json)\n"
    "\n"
    "For an annotated function whose wall is the order of float operations (commuted products, another sum order,\n"
    "/fp:fast reassociating): build the unit, read the float operation trees out of the machine code (the\n"
    "reference's at the annotated address, ours from the build), and classify every reference add/sub/mul/div node\n"
    "against ours:\n"
    "  match    some node of ours has the same operation and the same operand order\n"
    "  commute  the same up to the order of the operands of an add / mul\n"
    "  assoc    the same up to association and sign form ((a+b)+c / a+(b+c), a-b / a+(-b))\n"
    "  absent   no node of ours is that formula (another formula, factored, a constant folded, other leaves)\n"
    "FScore = (absent, assoc, commute); (0, 0, 0) = every reference node's exact order is produced. A candidate's\n"
    "rank is (FScore, extra, the scorer's score: status, differing bytes, dissimilarity); extra = operations of ours\n"
    "(add/sub/mul/div, neg/abs) that match no reference node, so a spelling that adds operations the reference lacks\n"
    "does not win on code length alone.\n"
    "\n"
    "The body's float expressions (sites: maximal trees of + - * / over atoms) are rewritten in place into\n"
    "algebraically equal spellings, with the moves: commute a + or *; reassociate; every order of a 3-4 term\n"
    "sum or product (left chains and balanced pairs); factor / distribute; sign forms (a - b, -(b - a), a + -b);\n"
    "x * 0.5f <-> x / 2.0f; x += e <-> x = x + e <-> x = e + x; s = a + b + c <-> s = a; s += b; s += c; the\n"
    "inlining of a single-use float local. No spelling introduces a local, a cast or volatile; an expression\n"
    "with two calls is never reordered. The function's braces must be on lines of their own.\n"
    "\n"
    "Phases (--minutes is the budget): A baseline (and the move set from the classification: only `commute` nodes\n"
    "off -> commutes and compound forms; only `assoc` -> also association, sums, signs; any `absent` -> all);\n"
    "B probe: up to 6 neighbouring spellings per site; a site none of whose spellings changes our operation orders\n"
    "is `insensitive` (the compiler canonicalises it) and is left alone; C per site, all spellings (BFS, at most\n"
    "--max-site) on top of the best body so far, keep the best, then another pass; the statement moves.\n"
    "Output goes under <build_dir>/float_order/<Name>_<address>/: result.json, state<k>_<tag>.diff.\n"
    "\n"
    "result.json: status exact / improved / none / insensitive / unparsed / no-float / error; base and best\n"
    "(FScore + score), tried, failed, sites, sensitive, insensitive_sites, states, game_nodes (counts by class\n"
    "before / after), exact_other (per other target: whether the best body is exact there too), unreached: the\n"
    "reference nodes whose exact operand order appeared in NO built candidate, rendered with their class against the\n"
    "best state. That list is the bounding evidence for a stop reason (\"the reference computes (a*a) + (b*b); N\n"
    "spellings of M sites built, none produces it\").\n"
    "\n"
    "With no float add/sub/mul/div in either the reference's function or ours the status is `no-float` and nothing\n"
    "is searched; with FScore (0, 0, 0) the search gets a third of the budget (the wall is elsewhere).\n"
    "\n"
    "Batch: every result of the adapter (unitcmp) that is not a MATCH and whose wall is --wall (default body), one\n"
    "child process each, --jobs at a time (default: CPUs / --workers); <build_dir>/float_order/summary.md and\n"
    "summary.json. --select filters on the stop reason.\n"
    "\n"
    "Priority: the search and its compilers run BELOW_NORMAL, so other work on the machine keeps the CPU first;\n"
    "--normal-priority or DECOMPKIT_SEARCH_PRIORITY=normal keeps the normal class.\n"
    "\n"
    "A result is evidence, never source: rewrite the found spelling by hand as the smallest authentic change and\n"
    "confirm it with the project's own compare.\n"
